Below is a detailed architectural and implementation plan for the "Cats Dealer" service. The solution prioritizes clean design, extensibility (Open/Closed Principle), robust error handling, and testability.

1. Technology Stack
Language: Ruby (3.x)
Framework: Sinatra — lightweight DSL for creating API-only services, perfect for this task without Rails overhead.
HTTP Client: Faraday — flexible middleware-based client with built-in timeouts and retries.
XML Parsing: Nokogiri — industry standard for parsing XML in Ruby.
Testing: RSpec + WebMock/WebStubs — to isolate external HTTP calls during tests.
Configuration: dotenv gem for environment variables (e.g., shop endpoints).
2. Project Structure & Clean Design

The code will be organized following PORO (Plain Old Ruby Object) principles. Business logic lives outside controllers; adapters handle third-party specifics.

