3. Domain Layer: Data Objects and Logic

app/domain/cat.rb
A simple immutable value object using Struct. It ensures data consistency across different sources.

ruby
Копировать
# frozen_string_literal: true

Cat = Struct.new(:id, :name, :breed, :price, :shop_name, keyword_init: true) do
  validates :price, numericality: { greater_than_or_equal_to: 0 }
end

app/domain/dealer.rb
The core business logic. It doesn't know about HTTP or JSON/XML. It only knows how to compare prices. This makes it trivial to unit test.

ruby
Копировать
# frozen_string_literal: true

class Dealer
  def initialize(adapters)
    @adapters = adapters
  end

  # customer_location can be used later for shipping costs calculation
  def find_best_deal(customer_location:)
    deals = []
    
    @adapters.each do |adapter|
      begin
        deals.concat(adapter.fetch_available_cats)
      rescue StandardError => e
        # Log the error but don't stop the whole process
        warn "[#{adapter.class.name}] Failed to fetch cats: #{e.message}"
      end
    end

    return nil if deals.empty?

    deals.min_by(&:price)
  end
end
4. Infrastructure Layer: Adapters and Error Handling

This layer isolates dirty work (parsing, networking). Each new shop requires only a new adapter inheriting from AdapterBase.

app/infrastructure/http_client.rb
Centralized place for time-outs and common headers.

ruby
Копировать
require 'faraday'

class HttpClient
  DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 5

  def self.connection(base_url:, read_timeout: DEFAULT_TIMEOUT, open_timeout: DEFAULT_TIMEOUT)
    Faraday.new(url: base_url) do |conn|
      conn.options.read_timeout = read_timeout
      conn.options.open_timeout = open_timeout
      conn.response :raise_error
      conn.adapter Faraday.default_adapter
    end
  end
end

